      "timestamp_raw": "May 13, 2015 0:02:01 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "glad you like them Eric!  Here's some more pics of various clones, check out the slight differences between the individuals.  Photos taken 5/12/15:<br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7726/17395269838_b3936b9234_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7747/17556681336_c84377a88e_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>The red throat almost looks like a burning red flame(I know, it's a little extreme comparison, but so is this plant, hehe):<br/><img src=\"https://c1.staticflickr.com/9/8800/16962767213_0fec7b8f7a_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>Most of these traps fell over in the move.  I tried to take pictures of multiple traps together for effect, but this was the best I could do:<br/><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/6/5337/17395551570_e2fda8f70c_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>S. flava killer has competition:<br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7747/17580832692_58d7b567c1_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7763/17395361168_2e253d2d8f_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/6/5470/17396850449_07c34e6c93_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7793/17583210665_0af77579c9_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c4.staticflickr.com/8/7686/17395656560_596258c969_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/6/5348/16962915603_3a9841ea21_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>This trap was bent, but still worth seeing:<br/><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/6/5336/17583285595_9e82c190e6_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>I love this one, there's something about it:<br/><img src=\"https://c2.staticflickr.com/6/5344/17396978389_b22985dc82_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>",
